.TH EL_INIT 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
el_init, el_end, el_reset \- initialize and reset editline state
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.BI "EditLine *el_init(const char *prog, FILE *fin, FILE *fout, FILE *ferr);"
.br
.BI "void el_end(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "void el_reset(EditLine *el);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR el_init ()
creates an editline session object and binds it to the three stdio streams
used for input, output, and diagnostics.
.PP
.I prog
is used in diagnostics and configuration context.
.BR el_end ()
releases all resources associated with
.IR el .
.PP
.BR el_reset ()
restores runtime state to default editor, keymap, and terminal settings
without destroying the session object.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR el_init ()
returns a valid
.B EditLine
pointer on success. On failure, NULL is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.PP
.BR el_end ()
and
.BR el_reset ()
return no value.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
One or more arguments were invalid.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Memory allocation failed.
.TP
.B ENOTTY
The configured input stream is not a tty and terminal mode setup failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR editline (3),
.BR el_gets (3),
.BR el_set (3),
.BR history (3)
